From b66f02b5738c7afb74cf5d3c9be83bbdf2cf07f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:41:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Ordered assembly: fixes of an independent review

- addStiffnessMatricesByRows: empty stiffness matrices refused before a
  division by zero; rows which do not match the degrees of freedom of the
  elements detected by the kernel; required pattern documented.
- computeElementsRows: the rows are built in a local object, so that they
  are left unchanged on failure.
- MultiMaterialNonLinearIntegrator: explicit error when the stiffness
  matrices of all the elements do not fit in an array of MFEM in the
  ordered assembly; number of ordered assemblies
  (`getNumberOfOrderedStiffnessMatricesAssemblies`, also given by the non
  linear evolution problems), checked by the tests, so that an ignored
  parameter is detected on the CPU too; documentation.
- Guide of the computations by kernels: `TangentOperatorAssembly`
  parameter, ordered assembly, its cost in memory and the extent of the
  reproducibility (the products of hypre on several processes may still
  change the last digits); no effect with the stiffness matrices computed
  element by element.
